        <div>
          <h4 class="text-cyan font-bold font-mono text-sm mb-3">Recall</h4>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs text-dust">
            <p><span class="text-cloud">Shell hook</span> captures every command with repo, cwd, exit code, duration → writes to local <span class="text-cloud">SQLite</span> via <span class="text-cloud">Bun</span>.</p>
            <p>Commands are searchable immediately via <span class="text-cloud">FTS5</span>. Projects are detected via <span class="text-cloud">git repo hash</span>. Workflows are mined from session groupings.</p>
            <p class="text-dust/60 mt-2">Zero network calls. One file at <code class="text-cloud text-[10px]">~/.recall/recall.db</code>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-dust font-bold font-mono text-sm mb-3">Atuin</h4>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs text-dust">
            <p><span class="text-cloud">Shell hook</span> (Rust) captures command + metadata → writes to local <span class="text-cloud">SQLite</span>.</p>
            <p>Optionally syncs to a <span class="text-cloud">server</span> (self-hosted or cloud) with <span class="text-cloud">client-side encryption</span>. History is available on any connected machine.</p>
            <p class="text-dust/60 mt-2">Database at <code class="text-cloud text-[10px]">~/.local/share/atuin/</code>. Sync requires a server or their hosted service.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-dust font-bold font-mono text-sm mb-3">fzf</h4>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs text-dust">
            <p><span class="text-cloud">No daemon, no persistence.</span> Reads <span class="text-cloud">stdin</span> and returns a selection. For history, it reads your shell's <span class="text-cloud">HISTFILE</span> directly.</p>
            <p>No metadata, no database, no background process. The shell integration is a shell function that pipes the history file into fzf's filter.</p>
            <p class="text-dust/60 mt-2">Depends entirely on your shell's history mechanism. What the shell saves, fzf can search.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
